    "question": {
      "source_id": "unreconciled:step-q213175",
      "problem": "Given that $w≡z\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8),$ construct a statement that also must be true:\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}w≡{{field-2}}z\\,(\\text{mod}{{field-3}})\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The scalar multiplication properties of congruences state that for $k\\in Z,$ we have the following:\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟹\\,ka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟹\\,ka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)$\n\nLet's multiply our congruence by $2$ and apply the second property.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w≡z\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)\\, & ⟹\\,2\\cdot w≡2\\cdot z\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2\\cdot 8) \\\\ w≡z\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)\\, & ⟹\\,2w≡2z\\,(\\text{mod}\\,16)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
